    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656">

                <pb facs="0788" n="692" xml:id="pg692"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to the Duke de Arcos.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 69.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise you that the
                    Secretary of War has received a telegram, dated the 17th instant, from General
                    Otis, stating that the <hi rendition="#italic">Alicante</hi> with 88 Spanish
                    officers and 1,039 enlisted men, released prisoners, sailed for Spain on the
                    13th instant; that 1,500 are still at Manila awaiting shipment, and that
                    probably 700 will be released in the south.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
